      "source_numbers": ["1079"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "multiple",
        "stem": "图中每行表示三个互不重合的点 $A(x)$、$B(x^2)$、$C(x^3)$，箭头向右。各行间距只是示意。给每行补上 $-1$、$0$、$1$ 后，下列次序中哪些可能成立？选择所有可能的方案；一行只需有某个实数 $x$ 能实现该方案。",
        "figure_ids": ["fig-67"],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "a)：$-1<0<1<A<B<C$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "b)：$C<A<-1<0<1<B$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "c)：$-1<0<C<B<A<1$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "D", "text": "d)：$-1<A<C<0<B<1$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "E", "text": "e)：$-1<0<B<C<A<1$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "F", "text": "f)：$-1<0<B<A<C<1$。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Jointly recognize feasible orders of x,x^2,x^3 across all six source rows and the complete placement of -1,0,1 for every possible row.",
        "source_solution": "a corresponds to x>1, b to x<-1, c to 0<x<1, d to -1<x<0, with the marker orders in those options. At x=-1,0,1 at least two source points coincide. If B<A then 0<x<1 and C<B, excluding e and f. No exact gap ratio is asserted.",
        "unit_reason": "One native multiple question retains the shared definition and all six diagram judgments, rather than separate yes/no clicks or pair-combination codes. Each feasible-row selection also identifies all three requested reference marks; no second question leaks the feasibility results.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": ["Recognition of completed strict orders does not demonstrate independently drawing the three requested marks or deriving the case split in writing."],
        "figure_observations": [
          {
            "figure_id": "fig-67",
            "observation": "Reused actual old independent pixel/display evidence at ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/7a/evidence/resume182-4-hard-figure67/review-FIRST/review.md.record, not a new image opening. Current SVG hash27b5b3caba51bbee3aaa2293e309b6b1b00f8bc896b062c6f72e2b40ab6b1082. The complete six separate right-directed rows are a ABC,b CAB,c CBA,d ACB,e BCA,f BAC; no origins or unit ticks and no calibrated gaps. Old full640 and mobile both-end observations cover all labels/arrows."
          }
        ]
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["A", "B", "C", "D"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Take x=2: A=2,B=4,C=8, so -1<0<1<2<4<8. More generally multiplication by x>1 increases positive powers.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Take x=-2: C=-8,A=-2,B=4, so -8<-2<-1<0<1<4. For every x<-1, x^3<x<-1 and x^2>1.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Take x=1/2: C=1/8,B=1/4,A=1/2, so -1<0<1/8<1/4<1/2<1. For 0<x<1, multiplication by x shrinks positive values.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "D", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Take x=-1/2: A=-1/2,C=-1/8,B=1/4, so -1<-1/2<-1/8<0<1/4<1. For -1<x<0, cubing retains negativity and shrinks magnitude, while squaring is positive below1.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "E", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "B<A would force0<x<1, where the actual C=x^3 is below B=x^2, not above it. Swapping the B and C coordinate assignments at x=1/2 gives the mistaken B=1/8,C=1/4,A=1/2 and exactly this false order.", "misconception": "Interchange the assignments of the square and cube between B and C when labeling the three powers."},
          {"option_id": "F", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "B<A forces0<x<1, so C<B<A, contradicting A<C. Misreading the exponent3 in C=x^3 as a cube-root instruction gives B=1/4,A=1/2,C=cuberoot(1/2), which lies between1/2 and1 and generates this false order.", "misconception": "Replace the third power by the third root while keeping A=x and B=x^2."}
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
